(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)={t}^{2}+1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364634 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c2ec86a9-5d87-5c18-b457-bd17da5e552f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364634 #edb/ref 1074 "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}+1)-(-\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{2}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{4}{3}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{56}{15}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364637 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364639 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186364640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186364640 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364635 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9e415229-8430-5c71-8b3d-4d06654a0d86" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364636 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364636 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364636 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2f65503b-cf8e-52cc-b535-c4e4ac1577d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186364637 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417